For \(u\in C^2(\Omega;\mathbb R^n)\), \[\operatorname{Div}(\operatorname{cof}
abla u)=0\] row-wise and \[\det
abla u= rac1n\operatorname{div} ig((\operatorname{cof}
abla u)^Tu ig).\] Thus, whenever the divergence theorem and traces are justified, \(\int_\Omega\det
abla u\,dx\) is determined by boundary data. Corresponding distributional identities hold under suitable Sobolev integrability.
